From 12b0e553f1c1450c32020fc3f91c56cd9d7c75e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 07:49:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(packs): consolidate the mission tier into one
 mission-type file per type

Migrates the built-in, cave-kitty and qa mission tiers to the sanitized
shape of spec-kitty-charter ADR-0044 (#194 PR-B), written by the charter
service's own writer:

- missions/<type>/<type>.mission-type.yaml holds the type, its steps in run
  order (steps) and the steps invoked on demand (on_demand_steps), each with
  its role, one-line description, expected outputs, output templates and
  references;
- missions/<type>/steps/<step>.prompt.md and .guidelines.md hold each step's
  prompt and working notes; a prompt keeps its frontmatter description as
  its detailed description, byte for byte;
- mission_types/*.yaml, mission.yaml, mission-runtime.yaml,
  governance-profile.yaml, expected-artifacts.yaml, actions/*/index.yaml,
  mission-steps/** and command-templates/* are retired (153 files); their
  YAML comments are not carried;
- the qa and cave-kitty DRG fragments name the new type files;
- packs/built-in.source.yaml carries the re-seeded tree_digest;
- docs/packs/ is regenerated, and the vocabulary guard drops the provenance
  row of the retired documentation governance profile.

Every decision the mapping made is listed in the charter mission's
migration report; the open-packs issues name each class of change.

Co-Authored-By: Stijn Dejongh <stijn.dejongh@sddevelopment.be>
