-# Schema C — the runtime MissionTemplate `spec-kitty next`'s planner reads.
-# The eight step ids are the canonical ids the planner special-cases
-# (implement/review for work-package discovery, specify/plan for artifact-presence
-# guards); cave-dev's identity lives in title/description, never in id. Agent
-# profiles are the consumer's built-in engineering roles — cave-dev re-voices the
-# lifecycle, it does not ship its own personas. Every step cites
-# cave-sty-001-communication through CAVE_001; the per-step prompt restates the
-# canonical software-dev action in caveman voice.
-#
-# Summarises the built-in `software-dev` mission contract as of software-dev
-# mission-runtime version 2.2.0. The command templates re-state that contract as
-# prose; they do not reproduce it, and there is no mechanical link, so when
-# software-dev evolves these summaries must be reconciled by hand. If you bump the
-# pinned version, re-read software-dev's steps and prompts and reconcile.
-#
-# Runtime caveat (a CLI-level coupling this pack cannot fix): the per-WP iteration
-# and the step guards `spec-kitty next` runs for `implement`/`review`, and the
-# analysis-currency gate ahead of `implement`, are keyed to the built-in
-# `software-dev` family in the CLI. A `cave-dev`-typed mission does NOT get them
-# from the `next` loop — its `implement`/`review` steps advance as generic
-# single-shot DAG steps. The lane/worktree execution path (`spec-kitty implement
-# WP##`) is unaffected. To drive a WP-iterating, guarded run in the caveman voice,
-# run `--type software-dev` with CAVE_001 + the styleguide activated.
-mission:
-  key: cave-dev
-  name: "Cave Dev"
-  version: "1.0.0"
-steps:
-  - id: discovery
-    title: "Discovery (caveman)"
-    description: "Investigate before specifying; report findings outcome-first, quoted source verbatim."
-    agent-profile: researcher-robbie
-    depends_on: []
-    prompt_template: discovery.md
-  - id: specify
-    title: "Specify (caveman)"
-    description: "Write the spec. Acceptance criteria precise and complete; surrounding prose terse."
-    agent-profile: analyst-annie
-    depends_on: [discovery]
-    prompt_template: specify.md
-  - id: plan
-    title: "Plan (caveman)"
-    description: "Produce the implementation plan; decisions stated outcome-first."
-    agent-profile: planner-priti
-    depends_on: [specify]
-    prompt_template: plan.md
-  - id: tasks
-    title: "Tasks (caveman)"
-    description: "Decompose into work packages."
-    agent-profile: planner-priti
-    depends_on: [plan]
-    prompt_template: tasks.md
-  - id: analyze
-    title: "Analyze (caveman)"
-    description: "Cross-artifact consistency and readiness check before implement; verdict outcome-first, references exact."
-    agent-profile: reviewer-renata
-    depends_on: [tasks]
-    prompt_template: analyze.md
-  - id: implement
-    title: "Implement (caveman)"
-    description: "Build the work package; progress replies terse, code and commands exact."
-    agent-profile: implementer-ivan
-    depends_on: [analyze]
-    prompt_template: implement.md
-  - id: review
-    title: "Review (caveman)"
-    description: "Review the work; findings outcome-first, evidence exact, risks in full sentences."
-    agent-profile: reviewer-renata
-    depends_on: [implement]
-    prompt_template: review.md
-  - id: accept
-    title: "Accept (caveman)"
-    description: "Confirm the result against the spec and record the decision."
-    agent-profile: reviewer-renata
-    depends_on: [review]
-    prompt_template: accept.md
